EXT. CABLE CAR OVER SPLINTER GORGE - DAY

A red gondola dangles beneath a single steel cable. Below, white rapids. Above, a bruised sky. The car has been still for hours.

INT. CABLE CAR - CONTINUOUS

Cramped. Fogged glass. Cold. Four people in parkas.

ABEBE (50s, guide's badge, steady) sits with a radio on his knee. SOLVEIG (30s, mountaineering gear) checks the roof hatch. BIG MO (40s, shaved head, shaking hands) clutches the safety bar. TERESA (20s, camera round her neck) films the glass.

SOLVEIG
Two hours since the stall.

ABEBE
Rescue knows we're here.

BIG MO
Then why isn't anyone coming?

ABEBE
Because the wind is bad.

TERESA
(to the camera)
Day one. We are still alive.

SOLVEIG
Turn that off.

TERESA
It's evidence.

SOLVEIG
Of what?

TERESA
Of how scared we are.

BIG MO
I'm not scared.

He grips the bar tighter. The car sways. He swallows.

ABEBE
Everyone sit down. Slowly. Weight low.

They obey. The car steadies.

BIG MO
(muttering)
Don't look at the river. Don't look at the river.

SOLVEIG
Mo, you're doing fine.

BIG MO
I'm not.

ABEBE
Radio's picking up something.

He turns the dial. Static. A voice, thin and far away.

BILLIE (V.O.)
...hold on... coming up the line...

TERESA
Did you hear that?

SOLVEIG
Quiet.

The car shudders. A thump on the roof. Another. Dust sifts from the hatch.

ABEBE
Stay away from the door.

The hatch opens. A rope drops. Then boots. BILLIE (30s, orange rescue suit, harness clanking) swings in feet first, grinning.

BILLIE
Evening, folks. Everybody breathing?

BIG MO
You're real.

BILLIE
Last time I checked.

TERESA
How many of us can you take?

BILLIE
(brightly)
Well, that's the thing.

She unclips. Looks at the four of them. Her smile fades.

BILLIE (CONT'D)
The line's frayed, and it's holding my weight just fine. It won't hold yours.

SOLVEIG
What does that mean?

BILLIE
It means I came to tell you the other cars are gone. This one's next.

Silence. The cable groans.

ABEBE
How long?

BILLIE
Until the wind turns? Maybe an hour.

BIG MO
Then why come?

BILLIE
Because someone should be here.

TERESA
(to the camera, very quietly)
Day one.

Solveig takes the camera. Turns it off. She puts an arm around Teresa.

SOLVEIG
Okay. Then we use the hour.

ABEBE
Everyone give me your coats. We make a sling.

BIG MO
For who?

ABEBE
For whoever goes first.

Billie hands her radio to Abebe. He takes it and nods.

BIG MO
I'll go last.

SOLVEIG
Mo...

BIG MO
I'm done being scared of the river.

The car sways. They hold on.
